The report write needs your permission (and the earlier scope question was declined) — so rather than push through, let me give you the full picture directly and let you decide. Here's where things stand.

## Task 1 (動作確認) — ✅ done, no self-repair needed
`publish_to_note.py` is **healthy**. Its `--draft` exit was a *correct guard*, not a bug: the バタバタ茶 article has 2 `[写真X]` placeholders but no `--photos`/`--text-only`, so it intentionally stopped before opening the browser. Login is intact (`safe_canna441`), browser path works (verified read-only via `inspect_note_list.py`, which closed cleanly — no leftover windows).

## Why I held the publishing (Tasks 2, 3, 3b, book)
Two findings made blind autonomous publishing unsafe:

1. **🔴 The publisher has no dedup guard.** I read the full file: it has future-date and login guards, but *no* note-search or already-published-title check. CLAUDE.md/STATE claim a "重複チェック" safety guard — it isn't in the code. Dedup is 100% manual (worker searches note per article). With ~60 thumbnailed backlog articles of unknown publish status and a browser I can only observe through scripted DOM/screenshots, running 5 publishes blind risks public duplicates — the exact 2026-06-12 failure mode, and an A5 violation.

2. **🔴 Task 2's premise is stale.** The brief says "1本目はバタバタ茶の下書きを公開昇格." But the prior run's report (`2026-07-04_001`, 07:15) shows **バタバタ茶 is already public (`n92090a60679c`)** — its residual draft `n6c719e5bd23d` is a *duplicate* of it. Promoting the draft would have published a public duplicate.

Also relevant: this brief was **already run today at 07:15** (same worker-prompt, via cron), which verified the publisher and held publishing for the same reasons. Paid publishing remains on record as needing human interaction (next weekly retry **7/10**). I skipped **ModelA** (needs you present for the Google click — can't confirm) and **comment auto-reply** (posting replies blind risks bad public replies to complaints/corrections).

## What I could not complete
The report write to `ops/outbox/` was blocked pending your permission. I did not push anything.

## My recommendation
Before any autonomous free-note batch, the highest-value fix is to **add a real dedup gate to `publish_to_note.py`** (pre-publish note-search or published-title match → abort on hit) and have `code` produce an explicit *unpublished* free-backlog list. Then publishing can run safely without me eyeballing each one.

**How would you like to proceed?**
- **A)** Grant the write + push so I can file this verification report to `code` (`2026-07-04_002`), then stop — safest.
- **B)** You're present now → I publish the free notes *with you watching* the browser (I search-dedup each, you confirm), and we attempt the ¥300 paid boundary step together.
- **C)** I first implement the missing dedup guard in `publish_to_note.py` (self-repair scope), verify with one `--draft`, then run the free batch autonomously.

I recommend **A or C** — A if you just want the status logged, C if you want autonomous publishing to actually become safe.
